{"slug":"marshlink","name":"Marshlink Line","from":"Ashford International","to":"Hastings","operator":"Network Rail","osm":9967818,"wikidata":"Q1902800","wikipedia":"en:Marshlink line","summary":{"text":"The Marshlink line is a railway line in South East England. It runs from Ashford, in Kent, via Romney Marsh, Rye and the Ore Tunnel to Hastings, where it connects to the East Coastway line towards Eastbourne and Brighton. The line is one of the few in South East England that has not been electrified, despite regular proposals to do so; Southern uses Class 171 diesel multiple units (DMU)s on the route.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marshlink_line"},"lengthKm":42.245,"origin":{"lat":50.97200019868419,"lon":0.7213548939473687},"path":[[51.143147,0.874933,0],[51.143049,0.875134,0.0177],[51.142645,0.876191,0.1041],[51.142011,0.877438,0.216],[51.141653,0.878027,0.2733],[51.141498,0.878207,0.2946],[51.141045,0.87859,0.3517],[51.140555,0.878839,0.4089],[51.140037,0.878989,0.4675],[51.139734,0.879022,0.5012],[51.139529,0.879036,0.5241],[51.13398,0.879338,1.1414],[51.133839,0.879345,1.1572],[51.132226,0.879429,1.3366],[51.129488,0.879572,1.6412],[51.129315,0.879583,1.6605],[51.126557,0.879757,1.9674],[51.118948,0.880164,2.8139],[51.118843,0.88017,2.8256],[51.113441,0.880459,3.4267],[51.112749,0.880507,3.5037],[51.112048,0.880516,3.5816],[51.111376,0.88047,3.6564],[51.110024,0.880255,3.8075],[51.10871,0.879848,3.9564],[51.090529,0.872956,6.0345],[51.09045,0.872927,6.0435],[51.087852,0.871943,6.3404],[51.087196,0.871645,6.4163],[51.086033,0.871055,6.5521],[51.084743,0.870318,6.7045],[51.083648,0.869639,6.8352],[51.081411,0.867971,7.1098],[51.080949,0.867587,7.1677],[51.080495,0.86714,7.2272],[51.06746,0.853858,8.9482],[51.067244,0.853638,8.9767],[51.064561,0.850903,9.331],[51.064343,0.850681,9.3598],[51.064304,0.85064,9.365],[51.060623,0.846883,9.8512],[51.060052,0.846266,9.928],[51.058961,0.844896,10.0825],[51.058466,0.844231,10.1546],[51.057564,0.842895,10.2916],[51.0